IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulations 3 to 5 and 10 to 12: the form of an
-- application (3), who may apply for someone else (4), and the day on which the Minister's approval of an application for a
-- pension (5), a supplement (10.1) or an allowance (12) takes effect. Regulations 10 and 11 say when the Minister shall approve.
--
-- Facts decided by the Act (whether a person is qualified for a pension under sections 3 to 5, when a person became entitled to
-- an allowance under sections 19 or 21) arrive as plain inputs. A day the text calls "the date specified in writing by the
-- applicant" is optional, so it is a MAYBE DATE; with none given that limb drops out (fork F-5(1)(e) in NOTES.md).

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Forms for Applications`

-- src:37 | 3 (1) Where required by the Minister, an application for a benefit shall be made on an application form.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 3(1) (src:37)
GIVEN `the Minister requires the application for a benefit to be made on an application form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on an application form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1): the application has the form the Minister requires` `the Minister requires the application for a benefit to be made on an application form` `the application is made on an application form` MEANS
        (NOT `the Minister requires the application for a benefit to be made on an application form`)
    OR  `the application is made on an application form`

-- src:38 | (2) Subject to subsections 5(2) and 11(3) of the Act, an application is deemed to have been made only when an application form completed by or on behalf of an applicant is received by the Minister.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 3(2) (src:38)
GIVEN `an application form completed by or on behalf of the applicant has been received by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act deems the application to have been made` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 5(2) and 11(3) of the Act (piece oa1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2): the application is deemed to have been made` `an application form completed by or on behalf of the applicant has been received by the Minister` `subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act deems the application to have been made` MEANS
        `an application form completed by or on behalf of the applicant has been received by the Minister`
    OR  `subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act deems the application to have been made`

-- src:39 | 4 (1) Where the Minister considers that a person is unable for a sufficient reason to make a request for a reconsideration or to make an appeal, an application, a statement or a notice, the request for reconsideration, appeal, application, statement or notice may be made on that person’s behalf by a responsible person or agency.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 4(1) (src:39)
GIVEN `the Minister considers that the person is unable for a sufficient reason to make a request for a reconsideration, an appeal, an application, a statement or a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(1): a responsible person or agency may make the request, appeal, application, statement or notice on the person's behalf` `the Minister considers that the person is unable for a sufficient reason to make a request for a reconsideration, an appeal, an application, a statement or a notice` MEANS
    `the Minister considers that the person is unable for a sufficient reason to make a request for a reconsideration, an appeal, an application, a statement or a notice`

-- src:40 | (2) Where a person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Unemployment Assistance Act or the Canada Assistance Plan, an application for a pension may be made on behalf of that person by the appropriate provincial authority.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 4(2) (src:40)
GIVEN `the application is an application for a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Unemployment Assistance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Canada Assistance Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` `the application is an application for a pension` `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Unemployment Assistance Act` `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Canada Assistance Plan` MEANS
        `the application is an application for a pension`
    AND (   `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Unemployment Assistance Act`
         OR `the person is or has been in receipt of assistance pursuant to the Canada Assistance Plan`)

§§ `Approval of an Application for a Pension`

-- 5(1): "Subject to subsection (2)", where the Minister (a) is satisfied the applicant is qualified under sections 3 to 5 of the Act
-- and (b) approves the application after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval is effective on the
-- latest of (c) the day received, (d) the day the applicant became qualified and (e) the date the applicant specified in writing.
-- src:43 | 5 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where the Minister
-- src:44 | (a) is satisfied that an applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act, and
-- src:45 | (b) approves the application after the last day of the month in which it was received,
-- src:46 | the Minister’s approval shall be effective on the latest of
-- src:47 | (c) the day on which the application was received,
-- src:48 | (d) the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act, and
-- src:49 | (e) the date specified in writing by the applicant.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(1) (src:43-49)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Minister approves the application` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the day on which the Minister approves the application` `the day on which the application was received` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act`
    AND `the day on which the Minister approves the application` GREATER THAN (`the last day of the month containing` `the day on which the application was received`)

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(1) (src:43-49)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in writing by the applicant` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the date specified in writing by the applicant` MEANS
    `oa3: the later of` (`oa3: the later of` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act`) `the specified date or the day the application was received`
    WHERE
        `the specified date or the day the application was received` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date specified in writing by the applicant`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the application was received`
            WHEN JUST specified THEN specified

-- 5(2): where the applicant attained 65 before the day the application was received, the approval is effective as of the latest of
-- (a) the day one year before the day received, (b) the day the applicant attained 65, (c) the day the applicant became qualified,
-- and (d) "the month immediately before the date specified in writing by the applicant". (d) names a month, not a day: the encoding
-- takes the first day of that month (fork F-5(2)(d) in NOTES.md), the earliest day the phrase can mean. With no date specified the limb drops out; the day one year before stands in for it because it is already one of the candidates.
-- src:50 | (2) Where the Minister is satisfied that an applicant mentioned in subsection (1) attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received, the Minister’s approval of the application shall be effective as of the latest of
-- src:51 | (a) the day that is one year before the day on which the application was received,
-- src:52 | (b) the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years;
-- src:53 | (c) the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act; and
-- src:54 | (d) the month immediately before the date specified in writing by the applicant.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(2) (src:50-54)
GIVEN `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` `the day on which the application was received` MEANS
    `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` LESS THAN `the day on which the application was received`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(2) (src:50-54)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in writing by the applicant` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the date specified in writing by the applicant` MEANS
    `oa3: the later of` (`oa3: the later of` (`oa3: the later of` `the day that is one year before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years`) `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act`) `the month immediately before the date specified in writing, or the earliest day`
    WHERE
        `the day that is one year before the day on which the application was received` MEANS
            `the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `before` `the day on which the application was received`
        `the month immediately before the date specified in writing, or the earliest day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date specified in writing by the applicant`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day that is one year before the day on which the application was received`
            WHEN JUST specified THEN `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 1) `months after the month containing` specified

-- The two together, with "Subject to subsection (2)": nothing is answered when subsection (1) does not apply, because the
-- Regulations then say nothing about the day (not covered). Subsection (2) reads "an applicant mentioned in subsection (1)",
-- which the encoding takes to be an applicant who meets both (a) and (b) of subsection (1) (fork F-5(2) in NOTES.md).
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(1) (src:43-49)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(2) (src:50-54)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Minister approves the application` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in writing by the applicant` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the day on which the Minister approves the application` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the date specified in writing by the applicant` MEANS
    IF NOT (`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` `the Minister is satisfied that the applicant is qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the day on which the Minister approves the application` `the day on which the application was received`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` `the day on which the application was received`
         THEN JUST (`reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant attained the age of 65 years` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the date specified in writing by the applicant`)
         ELSE JUST (`reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became qualified for a pension in accordance with sections 3 to 5 of the Act` `the date specified in writing by the applicant`)

-- src:55 | (3) Where the Minister, under subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act, deems an application to have been made and approved, the Minister’s approval shall be effective on the day on which the person attained the age of 65 years.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(3) (src:55)
GIVEN `the Minister deems an application to have been made and approved under subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 5(2) and 11(3) of the Act (piece oa1)
      `the day on which the person attained the age of 65 years` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 5(3): the day on which the Minister's approval of the deemed application is effective` `the Minister deems an application to have been made and approved under subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act` `the day on which the person attained the age of 65 years` MEANS
    IF `the Minister deems an application to have been made and approved under subsection 5(2) or 11(3) of the Act`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person attained the age of 65 years`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:56 | (4) If the Minister waives the requirement for an application in respect of a person under subsection 5(4) of the Act, the Minister’s approval is effective on the day on which the person attains the age of 65 years.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 5(4) (src:56)
GIVEN `the Minister waives the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 5(4) of the Act (piece oa1)
      `the day on which the person attains the age of 65 years` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 5(4): the day on which the Minister's approval is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` `the Minister waives the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4) of the Act` `the day on which the person attains the age of 65 years` MEANS
    IF `the Minister waives the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4) of the Act`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person attains the age of 65 years`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Approval of Application for a Supplement`

-- src:89 | 10 Where the Minister is satisfied that a pensioner is eligible for a supplement under section 11 of the Act, the Minister shall approve an application for a supplement by that pensioner in accordance with that section.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 10 (src:89)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the pensioner is eligible for a supplement under section 11 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10: the Minister must approve the application for a supplement by the pensioner in accordance with section 11 of the Act` `the Minister is satisfied that the pensioner is eligible for a supplement under section 11 of the Act` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that the pensioner is eligible for a supplement under section 11 of the Act`

-- src:90 | 10.1 If the Minister waives the requirement for an application for a supplement in respect of a person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act, the Minister’s approval is effective as of the day on which the person attains the age of 65.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 10.1 (src:90)
GIVEN `the Minister waives the requirement for an application for a supplement in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 11(3.1) of the Act (piece oa1)
      `the day on which the person attains the age of 65` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 10.1: the day on which the Minister's approval of the supplement is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` `the Minister waives the requirement for an application for a supplement in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act` `the day on which the person attains the age of 65` MEANS
    IF `the Minister waives the requirement for an application for a supplement in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1) of the Act`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person attains the age of 65`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Approval of Application for an Allowance`

-- src:93 | 11 The Minister shall approve an application for an allowance for the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner or for a survivor where the spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 11 (src:93)
GIVEN `the spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11: the Minister must approve the application for an allowance` `the spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` MEANS
    `the spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act`

-- Which of subsections (2) and (3) can apply depends on who is applying: the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (2) or a
-- survivor (3).
DECLARE `reg 12: Applicant for an allowance` IS ONE OF
    `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner`
    `reg 12(3): a survivor`

-- src:94 | 12 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), where the Minister approves an application for an allowance after the last day of the month in which the application was received, the Minister’s approval shall be effective as of the later of
-- src:95 | (a) the day on which the application was received, and
-- src:96 | (b) the day on which the spouse, common-law partner or survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(1) (src:94-96)
GIVEN `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(1): the approval of the application for an allowance is after the last day of the month in which the application was received` `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` `the day on which the application was received` MEANS
    `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` GREATER THAN (`the last day of the month containing` `the day on which the application was received`)

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(1) (src:94-96)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the spouse, common-law partner or survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 12(1): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse, common-law partner or survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` MEANS
    `oa3: the later of` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse, common-law partner or survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act`

-- src:97 | (2) Where the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attains the age of 60 years before the day on which the application for an allowance in respect of the spouse or common-law partner is received, the approval of the application by the Minister shall be effective as of the latest of
-- src:98 | (a) the day that is one year before the day on which the application was received,
