`reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` `the day on which the application was received` MEANS
    `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` LESS THAN `the day on which the application was received`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(2) (src:97-100)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner became entitled to an allowance under section 19 of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner became entitled to an allowance under section 19 of the Act` MEANS
    `oa3: the later of` (`oa3: the later of` (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `before` `the day on which the application was received`) `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years`) `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner became entitled to an allowance under section 19 of the Act`

