`reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act` `the day on which the application was received` MEANS
    `the day on which the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act` LESS THAN `the day on which the application was received`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(3) (src:101-103)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act` MEANS
    `oa3: the later of` (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `before` `the day on which the application was received`) `the day on which the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act`

-- All three together. Subsection (2) and (3) apply "where" their own condition holds, whenever the Minister approves (neither
-- repeats the condition of subsection (1) that the approval comes after the month of receipt); subsection (1) is "subject to"
-- both, so it answers only when neither applies and the approval comes after the last day of the month of receipt. When nothing
-- applies the Regulations say nothing about the day (not covered).
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(1) (src:94-96)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(2) (src:97-100)
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 12(3) (src:101-103)
GIVEN `the applicant for the allowance` IS A `reg 12: Applicant for an allowance`
      `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `the applicant for the allowance` `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the applicant for the allowance`
    WHEN `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` THEN
        IF `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` `the day on which the application was received`
        THEN JUST (`reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner attained the age of 60 years` `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act`)
        ELSE `the answer of subsection (1), if it applies`
    WHEN `reg 12(3): a survivor` THEN
        IF `reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act before the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act` `the day on which the application was received`
        THEN JUST (`reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act`)
        ELSE `the answer of subsection (1), if it applies`
    WHERE
        `the answer of subsection (1), if it applies` MEANS
            IF `reg 12(1): the approval of the application for an allowance is after the last day of the month in which the application was received` `the day on which the Minister approves the application for an allowance` `the day on which the application was received`
            THEN JUST (`reg 12(1): the day on which the approval is effective` `the day on which the application was received` `the day on which the applicant became entitled to an allowance under section 19 or 21 of the Act`)
            ELSE NOTHING
